  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Deepak Shrivastava vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 4 October, 2019 Author: Sheel Nagu Bench: Sheel Nagu 1 Mcrc 40254/19 The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Mcrc 40254/19 (Deepak Shrivastava Vs. State of M.P. )",
    "facts": "The petitioner has filed this first application u/S. 439 of Cr.P.C. for grant of bail. The petitioner has been arrested on 30/8/2019 by Police Station STF Bhopal Unit Gwalior (M.P.), in connection with Crime No.11/2019 registered in relation to the offences punishable u/Ss.420, 272,273, 120-B IPC & Sec. 51/59 of the Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006. Learned Public Prosecutor for the State opposed the application and prayed for its rejection by contending that on the basis of the allegations and the material available on record, no case for grant of bail is made out. Petitioner is alleged with managing dairy where certain material for preparation of synthetic milk was found. Investigation in the mater is over and therefore further custodial interrogation may not be necessary. In case the petitioner is unable to afford incurring of such expenses, then he would obtain saplings/tree guard from the forest authorities (the concerned Forest Range Officer of the area) free of cost or at concessional/nominal rates available under any beneficial scheme of the Government.",
